# Project contracts

Full architecture: `CLAUDE.md` at repo root. These invariants are non-negotiable.

## Stage API

Every pipeline stage is `run(config) -> tuple[int, Path]` writing one JSON manifest.

- Exit codes: `0` success, `1` policy/data failure, `2` invalid CLI/config
- Last stdout line of every CLI command: absolute path of the artifact written
- Never return `None` or print the artifact path elsewhere

## Idempotent reuse (`pipeline/rgb_pipeline.py`)

When changing stage behavior, update reuse predicates or the orchestrator silently keeps stale outputs:

- `_can_reuse_index`: year range, bbox, srs, strict/min, **provider**, geoportal **mode** (WMS-only stub vs real WFS), `wfs_bbox_axes_swapped` vs `geo.bbox.wfs_query_axes_swapped(srs)`, tile bboxes not axis-swapped
- `_can_reuse_download`: provider, mode/profile, `force_wms_years`, asset paths exist on disk

## Orchestrator

One entry: `pipeline/orchestrator.run(PipelineConfig) -> (exit_code, pipeline_manifest.json)`.
RGB defines `ReferenceGrid`; optional DEM/OSM align to it; optional `run_validate`.
`run_all.run` / `location_run.run_location` are thin wrappers preserving CLI return paths.

`run-all-location-json` skips a location only when `validation_report.json` has `passed=true` **and** `config_hash` matches `io.config_hash.run_config_hash(RunConfig)` for the current merged config. Missing/mismatched hash ⇒ do not skip.

## Downloads

Stream to `.part`, rename on success (`satmap_dataset.io.atomic`). Never write truncated files to final paths — reuse checks treat any non-empty file as complete.

## Configs

Construct via Pydantic models in `config.py`. New fields must default-resolve when missing from `base.json` or location JSON.

## Providers

RGB acquisition: `providers.get_provider(name)`. Registry includes geoportal, lantmateriet, sentinel2, lroc_nac, nls.
